{"id":"n2-021","title":"A。ということは B。 (A. To iu koto wa B.)","jlptLevel":2,"shortExplanation":"Expresses the meaning 'if A, that means B' or 'A implies B'.","longExplanation":"The A。ということは B。grammar point is used to express the logical conclusion that if A is true, then B must also be true. It can be translated as 'if A, that means B' or 'A implies B' in English. This pattern is used when the speaker wants to infer or deduce B based on the information provided by A.","formation":"A + ということは + B","examples":[{"jp":"彼女が泣いている。ということは何か悲しいことがあったに違いない。","romaji":"Kanojo ga naite iru. To iu koto wa nanika kanashii koto ga atta ni chigainai.","en":"She is crying. That means something sad must have happened.","words":[{"surface":"彼女","vocabId":"1483150","reading":"かのじょ"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"泣い","vocabId":"1229840","reading":"なく"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId":"1577980","reading":"いる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null},{"surface":"という","vocabId":null},{"surface":"こと","vocabId":"1313580","reading":"こと"},{"surface":"は","vocabId":null},{"surface":"何","vocabId":"1577100","reading":"なに"},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"悲しい","vocabId":"1483190","reading":"かなしい"},{"surface":"こと","vocabId":"1313580","reading":"こと"},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"あっ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"た","vocabId":null},{"surface":"に","vocabId":null},{"surface":"違い","vocabId":"1158870","reading":"ちがい"},{"surface":"ない","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}]},{"jp":"このケーキが残っている。ということは、みんなお腹がいっぱいだったのかな。","romaji":"Kono keeki ga nokotte iru. To iu koto wa, minna onaka ga ippai datta no ka na.","en":"This cake is left over. That means everyone must have been full, I guess.","words":[{"surface":"この","vocabId":null},{"surface":"ケーキ","vocabId":null},{"surface":"が","vocabId":null},{"surface":"残っ","vocabId":"1304510","reading":"のこる"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"いる","vocabId":"1577980","reading":"いる"},{"surface":"。","vocabId":nu